      <div type="clause" n="14.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 14.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="502–503" ed="#liebermann"/>E ki blasmé unt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_14-1.lnote.oe.b"/> esté, se escundirunt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_14-1.lnote.oe.b"/> par serment numé, ceo est a saver<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="bb" target="#LeisWl_14-1.lnote.oe.bb"/> par XIIII humes leals par num; s’il les pot aver, si s’en escundira sei duzime main.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="502–503" ed="#liebermann"/>Et altre qui blasmed ait<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#LeisWl_14-1.lnote.oe.6"/> ested, . . .<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#LeisWl_14-1.lnote.oe.7"/> per serment nomed, ço est a savoir quatorze<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#LeisWl_14-1.lnote.oe.8"/> homes leals per noun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#LeisWl_14-1.lnote.oe.9"/>; si il aver les pot, si s’en escondirad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#LeisWl_14-1.lnote.oe.5"/> sei dudzime main.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="502–503" ed="#liebermann"/>Quodsi ante culpatus fuit, purgabit se duodecima manu, et eligentur XIIII legales homines ex nomine, qui iuramentum hoc faciant.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="14.1" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="260" ed="#robertson"/>E ki blasmé unt esté se escundirunt par serment numé, ceo est a saver par XIIII humes leals par num; s'il les pot aver si s'en escundira sei duzime main.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="502–503" ed="#liebermann"/>14, 1. Und ein anderer, der [bereits früher] bescholten ist, (welche b. sind, sollen <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi>) soll sich reinigen durch [vom Gericht] ernannten Eid, d. h. durch 14<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_14-1.lnote.de.1"/> gesetzmässige Männer bei Namen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_14-1.lnote.de.2"/>: wenn er sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_14-1.lnote.de1.b"/> bekommen kann, so soll er sich davon reinigen selbzwölfter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_14-1.lnote.de.1"/> Hand.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">14, 1. And another who has been [previously] ill-reputed (those who are i. shall <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi>) shall clear himself by a nominated oath [nominated by the court], i.e. by 14 lawful men by name: if he can get them, then he shall clear himself of it with himself as twelfth hand.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="261" ed="#robertson"/>And those who have been (previously) accused shall clear themselves by the oath with selected compurgators, that is by means of 14 qualified men nominated [by the court], of whom 11 must act as the accused man's compurgators to clear him of the charge, if he can find as many to do so.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="503"><ref target="clause:IICn_65">II Cn 65</ref>; <ref target="clause:LeisWl_15">Leis Wl 15</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">vgl. ebd. 65 u. 15</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_15">Leis Wl 15</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 260–261 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 502–503, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_14-1.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Singular <hi rend="italic">bevorzugt MAT.; gemäss IL</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Singular preferred by MAT.; in accordance with IL</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_14-1.lnote.oe.bb" n="bb" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">saveir <hi rend="italic">bessert BA.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">saveir emended by BA.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_14-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">escoud. <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">escoud. Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_14-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">an <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">an Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_14-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze aus HkL</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply from HkL</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_14-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quacorte <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quacorte Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_14-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">non <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">non Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_14-1.lnote.de1.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">503</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">zur Eideshilfe willig</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">willing to act as oath-helpers</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_14-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">288</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> Auswahleid 1—e. 10. 12ff.; Eideshelfer 40. Zum Schwören willig müssen nur 11 sein, nicht, wie Schmid meint, alle 14</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See Gl</hi> Auswahleid 1—e. 10. 12ff.; Eideshelfer 40. Only 11 need be willing to swear, not all 14, as Schmid thinks</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_14-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">288</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Bedeutet diese Zufügung, dass das Institut der Glosse bedurfte, also veraltete? Oder tautologisch</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Does this addition mean that the institution needed a gloss, and was therefore becoming obsolete? Or is it tautological</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
